# v0.7.2 A: self-exclusion marker for agent-transcript-tailer.
#
# When RedLog is being developed IN itself (a developer runs `claude code`
# inside /path/to/redlog/), the tailer would otherwise ingest its own
# author's conversation into the engagement log — a feedback loop the
# adversarial-review agent flagged as Critical.
#
# The tailer walks up from each session's transcript-recorded cwd looking
# for this filename; if found anywhere in the ancestor chain, it skips
# tailing that session entirely.
#
# v0.7.4 F7: earlier revisions of this file mentioned an
# `enableSelfTail: true` config knob on AgentTailerConfig that would
# override the exclusion. No such knob exists in v0.7.x — the tailer
# skips self-marked sessions unconditionally. If you're a RedLog
# developer who genuinely wants their own dev session tailed, comment
# out the isSelfExcludedCwd() call in registerSession() locally.
#
# Committing this file (rather than writing it at Electron ready) keeps
# the marker in place for anyone cloning the repo, and avoids racing with
# runtime file creation.
